Make the copied Darwin framework writable

The Unpack targets copy Flutter.framework and FlutterMacOS.framework out of
the engine artifacts with `rsync --chmod=Du=rwx,...` and then thin the copy
in place with lipo. On macOS 15.4 and later /usr/bin/rsync is openrsync,
which accepts --chmod without applying it, so a copy from the read only Nix
store stays read only and lipo fails with "Permission denied" (reported as
"Failed to copy Flutter framework.").

Backported from Flutter 3.50, which runs `chmod -R u+w` on the copy.
See flutter/flutter#195257 and NixOS/nixpkgs#405066.

--- a/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/build_system/targets/darwin.dart
+++ b/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/build_system/targets/darwin.dart
@@ -57,6 +57,28 @@
         '${result.stdout}\n---\n${result.stderr}',
       );
     }
+    final String copiedPath = environment.outputDir
+        .childDirectory(environment.fileSystem.path.basename(basePath))
+        .path;
+    try {
+      final ProcessResult chmodResult = await environment.processManager.run(<String>[
+        'chmod',
+        '-R',
+        'u+w',
+        copiedPath,
+      ]);
+      if (chmodResult.exitCode != 0) {
+        printXcodeWarning(
+          'Failed to make the framework writable. This may cause the build to '
+          'fail when using lipo.\nError: $copiedPath: ${chmodResult.stderr}',
+        );
+      }
+    } on ProcessException catch (e) {
+      printXcodeWarning(
+        'Failed to make the framework writable. This may cause the build to '
+        'fail when using lipo.\nError: $copiedPath: $e',
+      );
+    }
   }
 
   /// Verifies and destructively thins the framework binary found at [frameworkBinaryPath]
